add('route-and-review','Jev Decides. Code Routes. Specialists Work.',90,'IN PRACTICE / OUR TRANSACTION WORKFLOW',`<div class="routing-workflow"><article><div class="workflow-step">1 · JEV CLASSIFIES</div><h3>What is the source?</h3><p>Transaction + supporting documents</p><div class="route-selected">Business</div><div class="route-alternatives">Inheritance · Employment · Gift</div></article><span class="workflow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><article><div class="workflow-step">2 · CODE ROUTES</div><h3>Choose the specialist</h3><div class="route-map"><div class="active"><span>Business</span><b>→</b><span>Business agent</span></div><div><span>Inheritance</span><b>→</b><span>Estate agent</span></div><div><span>Employment</span><b>→</b><span>Income agent</span></div><div><span>Gift</span><b>→</b><span>Gift agent</span></div></div></article><span class="workflow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><article><div class="workflow-step">3 · SPECIALIST ANALYZES</div><h3>Work through the case</h3><p>Use domain tools and, when needed, a reasoning model.</p><p>Return structured findings.</p></article></div><div class="live-review"><div><h3>Jev checks each result field against the original evidence</h3><p>Fast, low-cost checks as results arrive.</p><div class="review-fields"><span>Amount <b>supported</b></span><span>Payer <b>supported</b></span><span class="needs-review">Shareholding history <b>uncertain</b></span></div></div><span class="review-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="expert-review"><h3>Expert review</h3><p>Code flags uncertain or unsupported fields immediately.</p></div></div>`,"Return to our transaction. Jev decides the source category. Code uses that result to route the material to a specialist. That specialist can use domain tools and a reasoning model where deeper analysis is valuable.\n\nAs structured findings arrive, Jev can check each field against the original evidence. The amount and payer may be supported, while the shareholding history remains uncertain. Code applies the review policy and surfaces the uncertain field to an expert.\n\nThe model supplies judgments; code controls the workflow. Validate thresholds and end-to-end latency on the actual workload before deciding how much review to automate.",['routing','cascade']);

add('extract-by-choosing','Extract by Choosing',90,'IN PRACTICE / OCR FINDS TEXT · JEV IDENTIFIES ITS ROLE',`<div class="id-extraction"><article><h3>1 · Read the ID</h3><svg class="example-id" viewBox="0 0 380 250" role="img" aria-label="Identity card for Elena Rossi, born14May1988, expires2November2031"><defs><linearGradient id="id-paper" x2="1" y2="1"><stop stop-color="#f7f6ef"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#e9e8de"/></linearGradient></defs><rect x="2" y="2" width="376" height="246" rx="15" fill="url(#id-paper)" stroke="#c7c6bb"/><path d="M18 49H362" stroke="#e60000" stroke-width="2"/><text x="20" y="32" font-size="18" letter-spacing="2">IDENTITY CARD</text><rect x="20" y="67" width="100" height="129" rx="5" fill="#d5d6cd"/><circle cx="70" cy="106" r="24" fill="#999d93"/><path d="M30 185v-24a40 40 0 0 1 80 0v24" fill="#999d93"/><text x="140" y="79" class="id-label">GIVEN NAME</text><text x="140" y="103" class="id-value">ELENA</text><text x="140" y="126" class="id-label">SURNAME</text><text x="140" y="150" class="id-value">ROSSI</text><text x="140" y="176" class="id-label">DATE OF BIRTH</text><text x="140" y="200" class="id-value">14 MAY 1988</text><text x="20" y="230" class="id-label">VALID UNTIL</text><text x="140" y="232" font-size="18">02 NOV 2031</text></svg><p class="id-stage-caption">OCR preserves text and nearby labels.</p></article><article class="ocr-candidates"><h3>2 · Collect candidate spans</h3><div class="ocr-span"><b>A</b><span><small>Given name</small>ELENA</span></div><div class="ocr-span"><b>B</b><span><small>Surname</small>ROSSI</span></div><div class="ocr-span"><b>C</b><span><small>Date of birth</small>14 MAY 1988</span></div><div class="ocr-span"><b>D</b><span><small>Valid until</small>02 NOV 2031</span></div></article><article class="chosen-id-fields"><h3>3 · Jev matches the fields</h3><div><span>Given name</span><b>A → ELENA</b></div><div><span>Surname</span><b>B → ROSSI</b></div><div><span>Date of birth</span><b>C → 14 MAY 1988</b></div><div><span>Expiry date</span><b>D → 02 NOV 2031</b></div><p class="id-stage-caption">One Choice per field.<br>Include “not found” when no span fits.</p></article></div><p class="extraction-takeaway">Jev selects the span. Code copies the text and validates the dates.</p>`,"Start with OCR: it turns the ID image into text spans and preserves nearby labels. Jev receives those candidate spans and chooses which one belongs to each requested field.\n\nFor given name, choose A; for surname, B; for date of birth, C. Code then copies the selected text rather than asking the model to generate it again. Code also parses and validates dates.\n\nInclude a not-found option when no candidate fits. Choosing a span prevents inventing a value outside the candidates, but it cannot repair a bad OCR result automatically. The candidate quality and the matching quality are separate checks.",['extractChoice']);

add('closing','Give Intelligence the Right Interface',60,'THE TAKEAWAY',`<div class="closing-thought"><p>Keep the model’s knowledge.<br><em>Ask for the decision you need.</em></p></div><div class="closing-roles"><div><strong>Jev decides.</strong><span>Calibrated probabilities.</span></div><div><strong>Code executes.</strong><span>Rules, routing and validation.</span></div><div><strong>Reasoning goes deeper.</strong><span>When the case needs it.</span></div></div><p class="closing-question">Where does your system generate text just to make a choice?</p><div class="closing-links"><span>Let’s discuss.</span><a href="#/source-appendix">Sources ↗</a></div>`,"The takeaway is to give intelligence the right interface. Keep the model’s knowledge, ask for the decision you need, and use code to execute clear rules. Bring in deeper reasoning when the case calls for it.\n\nLeave the audience with the question on screen: where does your system generate text just to make a choice?\n\nPause and invite discussion for the remaining five minutes. Useful prompts: which decision could you test first, what would an error cost, and what evidence would persuade you to automate it? The source appendix is linked here.",[]);

add('source-appendix','Sources & Further Reading',30,'APPENDIX / SOURCE SNAPSHOT · 23 OCTOBER 2026',`<div class="source-directory">${[
  ['TypeSafe Jev', [['rlcd','Launch & System One'],['api','API & typed decisions'],['pricing','Models & pricing'],['parallel','Parallel questions'],['fanout','Speculative fan-out'],['rlcdPrimer','RLCD & machine-learning primer']]],
  ['Architecture & calibration', [['illustrated','The Illustrated GPT-2'],['inference','Prefill & decode · NVIDIA'],['transfer','Brown et al. · few-shot learning'],['calibration','Guo et al. · calibration'],['loraPaper','Hu et al. · LoRA'],['promptBias','Zhao et al. · prompt calibration']]],
  ['Open implementations & benchmarks', [['card','AutoTrust JEV-27B · model card'],['code','AutoTrust · implementation'],['temperatures','AutoTrust · fitted temperatures'],['semifCalibration','SemIf · calibration experiment'],['s1mb','S1MB · benchmark results'],['s1mbScoring','S1MB · scoring methodology']]],
  ['Practice & perspective', [['routing','Intent routing'],['cascade','Extraction & verification cascade'],['extractChoice','Extract by choosing'],['raschka','Raschka · Jev & generalization'],['openaiPricing','OpenAI · API pricing'],['medicalComparison','Jev vs reasoning · medical benchmarks']]]
].map(([heading, links])=>`<article><h3>${heading}</h3><ul>${links.map(([key,label])=>`<li><a href="${sources[key][1]}" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">${label} ↗</a></li>`).join('')}</ul></article>`).join('')}</div><div class="appendix-return"><span>Implementation and benchmark links use the revisions cited in the talk.</span><a href="#/closing">← Back to discussion</a></div>`,"Use this appendix during questions or after the talk. The links cover TypeSafe’s interface, the architecture explanations, calibration research, pinned open implementations, benchmarks and practical workflows.\n\nReturn to the closing slide for discussion. The source snapshot is dated so version-sensitive claims can be checked later.",[],{appendix:true});
